    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM proudly presents to the market this magnificent and beautifully appointed bungalow residence, located just a short distance from the world renowned village of Adare and the iconic Adare Manor Golf Club, set to host the Ryder Cup in 2027.\n\nThis hugely attractive four bedroom detached bungalow, constructed in1992 stands on a generous and beautifully maintained circa 0.51-acre site. The property offers spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout and is ideally suited as a family home. \n\nA particular feature of the property is the beautifully maintained south-west facing rear garden, which enjoys excellent privacy and is surrounded by mature hedging, established trees, lawns and colourful planting. The generous grounds provide an excellent outdoor space for entertaining, gardening or family use.\n\nInternally, the property is well maintained and offers four spacious bedrooms, a family bathroom and generous living accommodation. There is also extensive built-in storage, a floored attic and a detached garage with adjoining shed, providing excellent additional storage.\n\nThe location is simply second to none within moments of Adare`s picturesque main street, featuring excellent primary schools, boutique shops, renowned restaurants, chic coffee houses, and welcoming hosteleries.The Woodlands Hotel and Leisure Complex is just a 5 minutes walk away. The Adare Manor Hotel & Golf Club, one of the world`s premier golfing destinations is also on your doorstep.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a home that embodies style and an unbeatable location a perfect choice for those seeking a distinguished family residence in one of Ireland`s most desirable settings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hallway\nBright and welcoming.\n\nKitchen/living/dining room - 7.3m (23'11\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nTiled flooring. Built in gas hob. Patio door to rear garden.\n\nUtility room - 2.9m (9'6\") x 2.2m (7'3\")\nTiled flooring. Fully plumbed.\n\nSitting room - 4.2m (13'9\") x 4.1m (13'5\")\nLaminated flooring.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.6m (11'10\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\nLaminated flooring. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.6m (11'10\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\nLaminated flooring. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.6m (11'10\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\nLaminated flooring. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.7m (12'2\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nLaminated flooring. Built in wardrobes. \nEn Suite - 1.8m x 1m - Fully tiled. Triton electric shower.\n\nOffice/Bedroom 5 - 4.8m (15'9\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nLaminated flooring. Patio doors to rear.\n\nMain bathroom - 3.6m (11'10\") x 2m (6'7\")\nFully tiled. Mira electric shower.\n\nGarage - 6.9m (22'8\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\nW.C\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Double-glazed UPVC windows </li><li> Septic tank upgraded approximately 2 years ago </li><li> Beautifully landscaped gardens </li><li> Bright and spacious accommodation </li><li> Quiet and private residential setting </li><li> Generous tarmac driveway, set down and circulation area </li><li> Excellent range of living and bedroom accommodation </li><li> Unrivalled location </li><li> Great potential to develop and extend if required</li></ul>"
      },
